ILC1s are non-cytotoxic or weakly cytotoxic, expressing relatively low levels of perforin, and play an important role in the response to viruses, certain intracellular bacteria and parasites, and fungi. Their release of IFN-γ and tumor necrosis factor (TNF) further shapes the adaptive immune response. Their functionality mirrors Th1 helper cells.
